type: software
title: "Project Potimos: A Heuristic Framework for Frequency-Optimized Sonochemical Water Treatment"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-05-30
authors:
  - family-names: Zimmerman
    given-names: Carl
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >-
  Project Potimos presents a computational framework for optimizing
  sonochemical water treatment using a geometric constant Z = sqrt(32pi/3)
  approximately 5.79 Angstroms. The framework derives a candidate frequency
  of 517.9 kHz for PFAS degradation and proposes membrane mechanical
  resonance as the selectivity mechanism. This is a theoretical framework
  requiring experimental validation. Post-ultrathink analysis revised the
  original 220x synergy claim to 0.07x and identified transport-limited
  kinetics as the rate-limiting step. The probability of full theory
  validation is estimated at 5-10 percent.
keywords:
